invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64_addcarry.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh rsa-addcarry
reason: the form of the add with carry that x86-64 reads hands
  _addcarry_u64 a carry in of zero, so every block's chain drops the
  carries between its four words. CBMC reads the 128-bit sum form, so no
  proof covers this one, and an arm64 machine compiles that form too. The
  lane builds bin/rsa_addcarry_equiv_test for x86-64 on the intrinsic and
  runs it under qemu-x86_64, where it holds the rows to rsa_mont64.c's
  loops. The lane skips without docker, and this then reports unguarded
  rather than caught.

--- old
    return _addcarry_u64(carry, a, b, out);
--- new
    return _addcarry_u64(carry & 0, a, b, out);
